`bindHandleEvent` 每次都会 new 一个 ScreenSpac:
`bindHandleEvent` creates a new ScreenSpaceEventHandler every time and only cleans it up when the module is destroyed;
not destroying the previous one stacks them up: every button click adds a layer and a single left click fires several callbacks
(which shows up as observation points multiplying in a "nesting doll" pattern). This keeps only the last layer per instance.

与 `setPolygon()` 的关键区别：**不会再采样地形**。高度直接从:
Key difference from `setPolygon()`: **terrain is not sampled again**. Heights are restored directly from the payload,
so the pit is reproduced exactly even if no terrain service is configured at the moment or the original terrain has changed;
after loading, the brush, undo, statistics, water and contours keep working, and the ground texture is re-fetched for the new extent in the background.

250ms 比一般鼠标的移动事件间隔（8~16ms）大一个量级，即使设备掉到 4:
250ms is an order of magnitude longer than a typical mouse move interval (8~16ms): even if the device drops to 4fps and two `mousemove`
events are more than two hundred milliseconds apart, "still dragging" is never mistaken for "stopped";
at the same time it is short enough that the delay before digging starts is imperceptible.

被刷动过的顶点额外烘一层**方向性明暗**：迎光立面提亮、背光立面压暗。\n台阶:
Brushed vertices additionally get a **directional shading** bake: light-facing faces brighten, back-facing faces darken.
Steps are recognisable at a glance because of this abrupt shading change at the break of slope, not because of a different texture;
natural cliffs that were never brushed (zero displacement from base) are unaffected and keep the original imagery.
